{
  "_comment": [
    "Response shapes for collectors/dexscreener.py, used by tests/test_dexscreener.py.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE, stated plainly: these are hand-built to DexScreener's documented",
    "response schema. They were NOT recorded from the live API -- the session that",
    "wrote this module had no egress to api.dexscreener.com. So the parsers are",
    "verified against this file and the field names come from the documentation, but",
    "the shapes have the same status as the Bitquery query text in collectors/",
    "bitquery.py: written against a published schema, unconfirmed against the wire.",
    "",
    "Confirm and re-record on first run:",
    "    python -m collectors.dexscreener --probe --chains solana,bnb",
    "If a shape differs, replace the block below with the real response and the",
    "parser tests will point at exactly what has to change. The parsers are total --",
    "every field may be absent -- so a shape change degrades to nulls rather than",
    "crashing, which is the failure mode you want while this is unverified.",
    "",
    "The cases below are chosen to exercise the edges the parsers actually have to",
    "survive: numbers sent as strings, a token with two pools, a missing info block,",
    "a measured zero next to an absent field, a chain the registry does not know, and",
    "a pair whose baseToken has no address."
  ],
